{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"agent_message","text":"The first behavioral failure is confined to bytes beyond a merged buffer’s declared length inside `process_buffer_array`: C copies an uninitialized stack struct wholesale, so those tail bytes are indeterminate and cannot be a stable oracle. I’m narrowing that composed-operation assertion to the C-defined logical bytes plus length/checksum, while retaining full 256-byte comparisons for operations whose destination tail is initialized and observable; I’m also making the test mutex recover after a failed test so one divergence does not mask the others."}}
